<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS. [CORRECTED 22:47 GMT]</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS. [CORRECTED 22:47 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of first round second leg matches in African club soccer competitions:</p>
<p>Played Saturday:</p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Tunis: Etoile Sportive Sahel (Tunisia) 4 Etoile Filante (Burkina Faso) 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Imed Ben Younes 29, 64, Ryadh Jelassi 44, Ismail Peirera 63 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 25,000</p>
<p>Etoile Sportive win 4-3 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Cairo: Arab Contractors (Egypt) 2 Mumias Sugar (Kenya) 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Tamer el-Nahhas 3, Zizou 28</p>
<p>Arab Contractors win 2-0 on aggregate  </p>
<p>CAF Cup</p>
<p>In Rabat: Chabab Mohammedia (Morocco) 2 Horoya Conakry (Guinea) 1 (2-0)</p>
<p>scorers:</p>
<p>Chabab Mohammedia - Rahim Mohamed 16, Rachid Roki 18</p>
<p>Horoya Conakry - Foutouan Conte 78 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>Chabab win 2-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>Played on Sunday:</p>
<p>Champions' Cup (corrects from Cup Winners' Cup)</p>
<p>In Addis Ababa: St George (Ethiopia) 1 Zamalek FC (Egypt) 1 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>St George - Tesfaye Urgecho 34</p>
<p>Zamalek - Mokamed El-Kas 36</p>
<p>Attendance: 22,000</p>
<p>Zamalek win 3-1 on aggregate</p>
</text>
